<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31427" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŭmĭtōrĭus</span></b> ,
		a, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a Roman</i> gens. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> C. Numitorious, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 63, §
			163</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			L. Numitorius, <i>a tribune of the people</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 2,
			58</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			P. Numitorius, <i><span class="en">Liv. 3, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">54</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			Q. Numitorius Pullus, <i>a leader of Fragellæ
				in the contest of that city with the Romans</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Inv.
				2, 34, 105</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fin. 5, 22, 62</span></i>.—<i>His daughter</i> was named Numitoria, <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil.
				3, 6, 17</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
